ibution discloses.\",\"All five rows of the options table (ア/イ/ウ/エ) match the original: (1) SF₆ガス/エポキシ樹脂/低い/短い, (2) SF₆ガス/エポキシ樹脂/高い/長い, (3) 窒素ガス/磁器がいし/低い/長い, (4) 窒素ガス/エポキシ樹脂/高い/短い, (5) SF₆ガス/磁器がいし/高い/短い.\",\"The official answer table (電力 問6) gives 2, which matches officialAnswer=\\\"2\\\".\",\"The explanation is consistent throughout: SF₆ gas as the fill gas, epoxy resin spacers, high reliability because the equipment is sealed from outside air, and long restoration after an internal fault because the gas must be recovered, the enclosure opened and inspected, and the gas refilled.\",\"For each wrong option, the explanation correctly identifies which blanks are right and which are wrong: (1) ウ and エ wrong; (3) ア, イ and ウ wrong with only エ right; (4) ア and エ wrong; (5) イ and エ wrong.\",\"The only table is the options table, and it is fully transcribed into choices. There is no other figure needed to answer the question. officialReferenceUrls is empty. reviewedFromPage=[9] matches the page code T1-D 009.\"]},{\"unitKey\":\"20240818-power-q07\",\"questionNumber\":7,\"part\":null,\"status\":\"PASS\",\"textIssues\":[],\"choiceIssues\":[],\"answerIssues\":[],\"explanationIssues\":[],\"figureIssues\":[],\"sourceIssues\":[],\"verifiedEvidence\":[\"The question text and all five options (1) to (5) match the official original page (T1-D 010, printed page 7) word for word.\",\"The official answer table (電力 問7) gives 4, which matches officialAnswer=\\\"4\\\".\",\"The voltage-drop approximation ΔV≒√3·I·(R cosθ+X sinθ) is the standard form for a three-phase line, and the cause-and-effect reasoning is correct. Extending the line length (4) increases R and X roughly in proportion to length, which makes the voltage drop larger, so it is not a voltage-maintenance measure.\",\"The reasons given for the correct statements are specific to each option and correct: (1) sending-end voltage adjustment with LRT/LRA, combined with LDC where needed; (2) a phase-advancing capacitor reduces reactive current, and with the active current I·cosθ unchanged, the I·X·sinθ component falls; (3) a thicker conductor lowers R; (5) placing the transformer at the load center shortens the low-voltage lines.\",\"The original page has no figure, so figureUrls=[] and figureDescription are consistent with it. officialReferenceUrls is empty. reviewedFromPage=[10] matches the page code T1-D 010.\"]}]"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2042,"cache_read_input_tokens":164863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2042},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21a30195-73ac-4e7d-8efd-10503d1ddd43","uuid":"2ebe8ead-8f43-4664-8353-259022f2329d","timestamp":"2026-09-24T05:37:23.682Z","request_id":"req_011CfMivumxbac2gCyCubThY"}
